<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grammos</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mount Grammos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grammos is a mountain range on the border between north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and Albania, rising to about 2,520 metres. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-civil-war">Greek Civil War</a> it was the main stronghold of the communist Democratic Army, and in August 1949 the government army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandros-papagos">Alexandros Papagos</a> took it, together with nearby Vitsi, in the operations that ended the war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grammos.jpg" alt="Grammos" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kkostagiannis · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grammospeak.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
